                <pb facs="1068" n="972" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg972"/>

                <head>No. 674.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General Sickles to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-12-05"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 5, 1873</date>.
                        (Received 7.40 a.m., Dec. 6.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your instruction of yesterday received at 10.30 this morning. Interview with
                    minister at 3 this afternoon. He said order sent Wednesday to Polo directed him
                    to consult Minister Soler in Havana about place of surrender, and leave time to
                    be named by you. He said Polo had full authority to act as soon as place should
                    be determined. Minister said, in conclusion, he preferred to let his previous
                    orders stand, but he would direct Polo to lose no time in coming to an
                    understanding with Soler and signing further agreement with you.</p>
                <closer><signed>SICKLES.</signed></closer>
            </div>
